<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand II, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1578–1637</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand II, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>, was the son of Archduke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-archduke-of-austria">Charles II of Inner Austria</a> and ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graz">Graz</a> before becoming emperor in 1619. A Jesuit-educated champion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Counter-Reformation</a>, he expelled Protestant preachers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> and his other lands. The Bohemian revolt against him in 1618 began <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, and his victory at the White Mountain in 1620 was followed by forced re-Catholicisation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Ferdinand II, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Ferdinand_II,_Holy_Roman_Emperor_(Kunsthistorisches_Museum,_Wien).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
